<Layout>
	<section class="mb-5">
		<h1>MICRONEEDLING (ReNu Pen®)</h1>
		<p class="text-xl bg-[#EEE8E0] px-2">PRE-TREATMENT INSTRUCTIONS</p>
	</section>
	<section>
		<div class="separation">
			<h2>ABOUT MICRONEEDLING</h2>
			<p>Microneedling (ReNu Pen®) is a minimally invasive procedure that creates controlled micro-injuries in the skin to stimulate collagen and elastin production. This natural healing process improves skin texture, tone, and overall appearance.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>INDICATIONS</h2>
			<p>Microneedling may be recommended to improve:</p>
			<p>	• Fine lines and wrinkles (face, neck, and décolletage) <br>
				• Acne scars <br>
				• Post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation <br>
				• Enlarged pores <br>
				• Uneven skin texture <br>
				• Stretch marks (body applications) <br>
				• Hyperpigmentation and melasma (with caution) <br>
				• General skin rejuvenation and improved skin quality <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>BENEFITS OF MICRONEEDLING</h2>
			<p>Potential benefits include:</p>
			<p>	• Increased collagen and elastin production <br>
				• Improved skin tone and texture <br>
				• Softening of fine lines and wrinkles <br>
				• Improvement in acne scars <br>
				• Reduction in enlarged pores <br>
				• Improvement in stretch marks <br>
				• Enhanced absorption of physician-recommended skincare products <br>
				• Minimal downtime with gradual, natural-looking results <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>CONTRAINDICATIONS</h2>
			<h2>ABSOLUTE CONTRAINDICATIONS</h2>
			<p>	• Active acne breakout within the treatment area <br>
				• Active cold sore (HSV) or other active skin infection <br>
				• Open wounds or cuts within the treatment area <br>
				• Current isotretinoin (Accutane®) use or use within the previous 6 months <br>
				• Active eczema, psoriasis, or dermatitis within the treatment area <br>
				• Keloid scarring tendency <br>
				• Blood clotting disorders or active anticoagulant therapy <br>
				• Pregnancy (first trimester; clinical judgment during the second and third trimesters) <br>
				• Recent radiation therapy to the treatment area <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>RELATIVE CONTRAINDICATIONS</h2>
			<p>	• Rosacea (consider lower treatment depths and exercise caution) <br>
				• Fitzpatrick Skin Types V–VI (higher risk of post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation) <br>
				• Chemical peel or laser treatment within the previous 2 weeks <br>
				• History of keloid formation without active lesions <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>BEFORE YOUR TREATMENT</h2>
			<h2>TWO WEEKS BEFORE</h2>
			<p>	• Discontinue retinoids (tretinoin, retinol) and exfoliating acids (AHAs and BHAs). <br>
				• Avoid waxing or threading the treatment area. <br>
				• Minimize sun exposure and wear Mineral SPF 50 sunscreen daily. <br>
				• If medically appropriate, avoid blood-thinning medications or supplements (aspirin, ibuprofen, fish oil, vitamin E) only after discussing with your prescribing provider. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>DAY OF TREATMENT</h2>
			<p>	• Arrive with clean skin free of makeup, moisturizer, sunscreen, or skincare products. <br>
				• Do not receive treatment if you have an active breakout, cold sore, or skin infection. <br>
				• Inform your provider of any changes in your medications or health history since your last visit. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>QUESTIONS?</h2>
